# Permission Protocol Deploy Gate

> No AI agent deploys code without human approval.

Screenshot would show a pull request blocked by a failing `Permission Protocol Verify` check, an approval page with the pending request details and approve/deny controls, then the same PR turning green so the deploy can proceed.

## 30-Second Setup

### 1. Add the workflow

Create `.github/workflows/deploy-gate.yml`:

```yaml
name: Deploy Gate

on:
  pull_request:
    branches:
      - main

jobs:
  deploy-gate:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - name: Verify human approval
        uses: permission-protocol/verify@v1
        with:
          pp_base_url: ${{ secrets.PP_BASE_URL }}
          pp_api_key: ${{ secrets.PP_API_KEY }}
          environment: production
```

### 2. Set secrets

Go to Settings -> Secrets -> Actions and add:

- `PP_BASE_URL`: `https://app.permissionprotocol.com` (or your self-hosted URL)
- `PP_API_KEY`: Get one at https://app.permissionprotocol.com/settings/api-keys

### 3. Push a commit

That's it. The next PR will be gated.

## What Happens

```text
AI pushes code -> Gate blocks PR -> Human reviews -> Approves -> PR merges
     ❌                🔍               ✅             🚀
```

1. An AI agent (Codex, Claude Code, Cursor) opens a PR.
2. The deploy gate creates an approval request.
3. A human reviews the changes and approves or denies.
4. The gate passes and the PR can merge.
5. A cryptographic receipt proves who authorized it.

The action auto-detects the repository, PR number, commit SHA, ref, workflow run, and actor from GitHub context. In pull request workflows it verifies the PR head SHA by default, which avoids approval churn from GitHub's temporary merge commits.

## Inputs

| Input | Required | Default | Description |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `pp_base_url` | Yes | None | Permission Protocol API base URL. |
| `pp_api_key` | Yes | None | Permission Protocol API key in `pp_live_xxx` format. |
| `pp_request_create_token` | No | `''` | Optional trusted token that lets the verify endpoint create deploy-gate requests when no receipt exists. |
| `environment` | No | `''` | Deployment environment such as `production` or `staging`. |
| `artifact_digest` | No | `''` | Artifact digest or hash to bind the approval to a specific build output. |
| `capability` | No | `''` | Capability being requested, for example `deploy:production`. |
| `fail_on_missing` | No | `true` | Fails the action when no receipt is found. |
| `redeem` | No | `true` | Redeems the receipt during verification so it can be single-use. |
| `fail_on_signing_key_fallback` | No | `true` | Fails if verification only succeeds via the global signing-key fallback instead of the tenant-local key. |
| `commit_sha` | No | `''` | Overrides the commit SHA used for verification. |
| `ref` | No | `''` | Overrides the Git ref used for verification. |

## Outputs

| Output | Description |
| --- | --- |
| `valid` | Whether the receipt is valid. |
| `receipt_id` | Receipt ID when a matching receipt is found. |
| `decision` | Receipt decision such as `APPROVED`, `DENIED`, or `PENDING`. |
| `error_code` | Error code when verification fails. |
| `error_message` | Human-readable error message when verification fails. |
| `request_id` | Deploy-gate request ID when verification creates or finds a pending request. |
| `approval_url` | Approval URL for the pending request flow. |
| `signing_key_fallback` | Whether signature verification used the global fallback key. |

## Advanced

### Environment-specific gating

Run the same action in different jobs with different `environment` values:

```yaml
- uses: permission-protocol/verify@v1
  with:
    pp_base_url: ${{ secrets.PP_BASE_URL }}
    pp_api_key: ${{ secrets.PP_API_KEY }}
    environment: staging
```

```yaml
- uses: permission-protocol/verify@v1
  with:
    pp_base_url: ${{ secrets.PP_BASE_URL }}
    pp_api_key: ${{ secrets.PP_API_KEY }}
    environment: production
```

### Auto-approve for staging

If your staging lane should not block, skip the gate for that environment and keep the gate on production:

```yaml
jobs:
  deploy:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - name: Gate production deploys
        if: github.base_ref == 'main'
        uses: permission-protocol/verify@v1
        with:
          pp_base_url: ${{ secrets.PP_BASE_URL }}
          pp_api_key: ${{ secrets.PP_API_KEY }}
          environment: production
```

### Required status checks setup

In GitHub branch protection for `main`, require the deploy-gate job to pass before merge. That turns this action into an enforced approval boundary instead of an informational check.

## FAQ

- "What if I remove this action?" Requires modifying CI. Intentionally sticky.
- "Does this work with existing workflows?" Yes. Add it as one step before merge or deploy-sensitive steps.
- "What about non-AI deploys?" It works for all deploys. AI agents just make the approval boundary essential.
